==== Flashing Firmware ====

The firmware can be flashed from within the OEM web interface or…

==== Install via TFTP ====
See [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.tftp|TFTP Flashing HOWTO]] for more details

  - reset router to default factory settings
  - Unplug router power cord, just cycling the power with the power button does NOT work.
  - Keep reset button down
  - Plug the power cord back 
  - Release the reset button.
  - Blue LED blinks slowly when ready for flashing((If it doesn't start flashing try to give the put the .trx file command anyway, if too early or too late then it will time out.))
  - Assign your PC ethernet adapter the address 192.168.1.11/24.
  - Make sure your PC is connected to one of the **LAN ports** of the router, not the **WAN port**.
  - Use TFTP to upload the firmware\\ <code>
$ tftp 192.168.1.1
tftp> bin
tftp> put openwrt-15.05-bcm53xx-asus-rt-ac56u-squashfs.trx
</code>
  - Wait for the LED to stop flashing and for the device to reboot.
  - Then telnet to 192.168.1.1 or visit 192.168.1.1 with your browser to access the LUCI interface

==== Recovery ====
//untested//  but should work

  -  Download & Install the asus "Firmware Restoration" from asus website
  -  Download the factory image from asus
  -  Enter Recovery Mode
  -  Unplug Router
  -  Hold Reset Button and Plug in Router
  -  Release button when front LED flashes slowly
  -  Use the following to set up your TCP/IP settings:IP address: 192.168.1.x Subnet mask: 255.255.255.0
  -  Select firmware *.trx and upload

In Recovery Mode, there is an extremely rudimentary CFE web interface (at http://192.168.1.1) which can be used to flash firmware files (.trx) and to clear NVRAM.


